      "card_ids": ["C03","C13","C05","C01","C02"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for structurally related JAK inhibitors show measurable systemic exposure after oral dosing: ritlecitinib Cmax 152.6–272.3 ng/mL and AUClast 448.1 ng·h/mL (C61, C83, C97, C94), upadacitinib AUC0-24 525–582 ng·h/mL at 30 mg ER (C54, C80), delgocitinib AUC0-inf 957 h·ng/mL at 25 mg (C86), peficitinib Cmax 241.1–648.7 ng/mL (C57, C70), and oclacitinib plasma concentration 122.9 ng/mL at 10 h in cats (C64).",
      "card_ids": ["C61","C83","C97","C94","C54","C80","C86","C57","C70","C64"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L3 record provides affirmative evidence for F<20%; the rifampicin DDI reduction for ritlecitinib (Cmax 204.4 vs 272.3 ng/mL, C56) still leaves substantial exposure and does not contradict the threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C56"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
